  "title": "Magnuson Park",
  "indexDescription": "Magnuson Park in January 2008.",
  "description": "I walked down to Magnuson Park in January 2008 and took some artistic photos.  It was cold and icy.",
  "cNum": 32,
  "posted": "2026-09-20",
  "images": [
    {
      "description": "The Straight Shot art piece.  The rock blocks are lined up where surveyors calibrate their distance measuring devices.  It was newly installed at the time this photo was taken.  The blocks start closely spaced then get farther and farther apart, following a fibonacci sequence spacing.  The line spans the whole park.  One block wasn't installed until years later because it was in a marsh.  \n\nIn the background you can see where they keep the trees cut for a clear view through the park.\n",
